## Goal
Make Portero appear in System Settings > Desktop & Dock > "Default web browser" list, since the user saw only Safari there even though Portero was already the actual http/https handler.

## Problems
- After the DEV-25 merge, `portero default set` printed "already set" for both schemes while the user believed Safari was default. Launch Services records showed Portero had been the handler since the first `default set`.
- The System Settings picker did not list Portero at all, so choosing Safari there changed nothing.
- The picker caches its list, so System Settings had to be quit and reopened to see the change.

## Decision
Added `CFBundleDocumentTypes` for HTML (`public.html`, `public.xhtml`) to `packaging/Info.plist`, on a new branch `fix-browser-picker-listing`. macOS lists an app as a browser only if it declares HTML document types, as other browser routers do. Rebuilt and re-registered the app; Launch Services now reports the HTML UTIs and the http/https schemes as claimed. The user confirmed Portero now shows up in the picker.

## Rejected
None.

